* START-HISTORY:
* 21 Nov 26 Windows port - New.  RELEASE_1.1 382, the owner in chat: "A dialog specifying why a restart might be needed, warning that
*           everyone will be logged out and giving a Restart|Not now option would be the best", and "That should be true for any other full
*           screen action where a restart is needed to implement it".  Until now only the status line said so, which is easily missed.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $tk_restart(why, res, msg)
*
*     why   why this change needs a restart, one line to a field (the page's own words: which setting, and that SD reads it only when it starts)
*     res   returned: 'later' when Not now was chosen (or Esc, or no terminal); 'failed' when Restart was chosen and SD could not be restarted.
*           When the restart works this session is ended with every other, so nothing comes back.
*     msg   returned: the line for the page's status bar
*
*   The box: its title says "Restart SD?", then why, then that a restart signs out everyone using SD and ends this session too, then what Not now
*   means.  Two buttons, Restart and Not now; NOT NOW IS THE DEFAULT ($tk_confirm's last button is), so Enter alone never restarts SD.
*   Restart hands the restart to Task Scheduler (restart-sd.ps1 -Detach, a one-shot SYSTEM task, RELEASE_1.1 340), as REMOTE.API RESTART does,
*   because this session and its elevated helper end with SD.  Only an administrator's page calls this: the script runs through !ps_script_out.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine tk_restart(why, res, msg)
$catalog $tk_restart

$include int$keys.h

deffun ps_script_out(script, want.out) calling '!ps_script_out'

   res = 'later'
   msg = ''

   lines = why
   lines<-1> = 'Restarting stops SD and starts it again.  Everyone using SD is signed out, and this session ends too.'
   lines<-1> = 'Not now: nothing restarts, and the change takes effect when SD is next started.'
   call $tk_confirm('sd -restart', lines, '', cres, cmsg, 'Restart SD?', '&Restart,&Not now')
   if cres # 'run' then
      msg = 'SD was not restarted: the change takes effect when SD is next started'
      return
   end

   ps  =       '& ' : char(39) : kernel(K$WINPATH, '/restart-sd.ps1') : char(39) : ' -Detach'
   ps := @fm : 'exit $LASTEXITCODE'
   rs = ps_script_out(ps, @true)
*  When the restart works, this session has been ended before the script returns.  Reaching here with 0 means the stop is still on its way.
   rc = rs<1>
   if rc = 0 then
      msg = 'SD is restarting: this session ends'
      return
   end
   res = 'failed'
   last = ''
   rn = dcount(rs, @fm)
   for ri = 2 to rn
      if trim(rs<ri>) # '' then last = trim(rs<ri>)
   next ri
   msg = 'SD was not restarted (status ' : rc : ')' : (if last = '' then '' else ': ' : last)
   return
end

* END-CODE
